cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: Pipe Steady State Initializers
authors:
  - family-names: Myers
    given-names: Richard
abstract: >-
  A C++20 reference library for constructing steady starting states for
  transient single-pipe simulations. It compares analytical approximations,
  spatial marching, coupled steady Newton solves, and implicit theta
  relaxation across isothermal, adiabatic, thermal-wall, and soil-shell
  reference models.
keywords:
  - pipeline hydraulics
  - steady-state initialization
  - numerical methods
  - C++20
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/rdm375/PipeSteadyStateInitializers
